      {
        "question_text": "Calculate.\na. $4.27\\times6$\nb. $2.6\\times3.7$\nc. $0.024\\times0.05$",
        "solution_text": "a. $427\\times6=2562$. Use $2$ decimal places.\n$4.27\\times6=25.62$\nb. $26\\times37=962$. Use $1+1=2$ decimal places.\n$2.6\\times3.7=9.62$\nc. $24\\times5=120$. Use $3+2=5$ decimal places, including leading zeros.\n$0.024\\times0.05=0.00120=0.0012$"
      },
      {
        "question_text": "Calculate.\na. $7.56\\div4$\nb. $6.975\\div0.03$\nc. $3.17\\div0.6$, correct to $2$ decimal places.",
        "solution_text": "a. Keep the decimal point lined up when dividing.\n$7.56\\div4=1.89$\nb. Multiply both numbers by $100$ to make the divisor whole.\n$6.975\\div0.03=697.5\\div3=232.5$\nc. Multiply both numbers by $10$.\n$3.17\\div0.6=31.7\\div6=5.2833\\ldots$\nThe third decimal digit is $3$, so $3.17\\div0.6\\approx5.28$."
      },
      {
        "question_text": "a. Without a calculator, find the weekly pay for a worker who earns $\\$12.40$ per hour and works a total of $31$ hours in the week.\nb. Calculate $45.12\\div0.08$.",
        "solution_text": "a. $1240\\times31=38440$. The hourly pay has $2$ decimal places.\nWeekly pay: $31\\times\\$12.40=\\$384.40$.\nb. Multiply both numbers in the division by $100$.\n$45.12\\div0.08=4512\\div8=564$."
      }
    ],
